    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 26th with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97), who holds the slate\u2019s elite score thanks to a favorable matchup against Montero and an exceptional 0.448 xwOBA. He is joined in the \"elite start\" tier by **Trea Turner** (76.36), **Christian Yelich** (75.84), and **Kyle Schwarber** (75.51). These three capitalize on prime hitting environments against Thornton; specifically, the efficiency scores for **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** are bolstered significantly by a soft 5.20 xERA opposing starter and a favorable platoon setup. **Colt Keith** (67.60) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) represent our most efficient middle-infield options, with **Colt Keith** benefiting from a helpful platoon edge and **Casey Schmitt** enjoying a projected #3 spot in the order combined with a 5% wind-out boost at the park.\n\nWhile the depth is strong, we are closely monitoring the 35% rain risk for **Caleb Durbin** (54.34), whose efficiency is already tempered by a tighter matchup against Warren. The most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (45.02), who pushed hard for a utility spot but was ultimately kept out due to the daunting 3.14 xERA presented by Wheeler. Though **Carson Benge** maintains solid base metrics, the optimizer preferred the high-leverage spots currently occupied by **Junior Caminero** (71.42) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (60.10). Even with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** facing a challenging 2.74 xERA arm in Misiorowski, his stolen base upside remains critical to our 5x5 Roto strategy, forcing **Dillon Dingler** (54.09) and **Lars Nootbaar** (48.64) to provide steady production while we mitigate the risk of our bench pieces like **Chase Meidroth** or the currently inactive **Hyeseong Kim** and **Gary Sanchez**.",
